A man of the tribe of Asher living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.7.37; 
son of: Zophah (H6690); 
brother of: Suah (H5477), Harnepher (H2774), Shual (H7777B), Beri (H1275), Imrah (H3236), Bezer (H1221H), Hod (H1936), Shamma (H8037H), Shilshah (H8030) and Beera (H0878); 
father of: Jephunneh (H3312H), Pispa (H6462) and Ara (H0690); also called Jether at 1Ch.7.38; 
Another name of yit.ran…

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.17.25; married to Abigail (H0026H); 
father of: Amasa (H6021); also called Ithra at 2Sa.17.25;
Another name of ye.ter (יֶ֫תֶר "Jether" H3500H) 
§ Ithra = "abundance"
father of Amasa, the commander of Absalom's army; also 'Jether'

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Exo.2.18; 
father of: Zipporah (H6855) and Hobab (H2246); also called Reuel (KJV: Raguel) at Num.10.29; 
§ Jethro = "his abundance"
father-in-law of Moses; also 'Jether'

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.36.26; 
son of: Dishon (H1787); 
brother of: Hemdan (H2533), Eshban (H0790) and Cheran (H3763)
§ Ithran = "advantage"
1) an Edomite, son of Dishon, a Horite, and probably a phylarch of a tribe of the Horim
2) an descendant of Asher

